Track 2: Did You Sleep Through the Ferry Bell?
- Story & Context: Stranded in the dusty oasis outpost of Bir-Zayt, rhythm guitarist Leila confessed to her caravan elders that she had deliberately pawned the camp’s schedule ledger to buy a battered FM synth module from a passing dhow trader. She spent the sweltering dawn hiding behind the salt warehouse, smelling of spilled coconut oil and heated copper wire, working out an intricate syncopated acoustic strum pattern to blot out the harbor's departure horn. As the distant ferry sails shrank against the turquoise horizon, she sang in a breathless, high-lonesome mountain harmony, "I traded twelve clean hours for a box of singing wire." The track became a runaway anthem for every runaway caravan kid who ever chose a sparkling new riff over an honest itinerary.
